[
    Err(
        "x means another level on features-and-maintenance/b; move it with --severity <level>",
    ),
    Err(
        "y means another level on features-and-maintenance/b; move it with --severity <level>",
    ),
    Err(
        "major is not on the scale of features-and-maintenance/nav; move it with --severity <level>",
    ),
    Err(
        "raising from z needs --scenario <reproduction or failure scenario>",
    ),
    Err(
        "raising from major needs --scenario <reproduction or failure scenario>",
    ),
    Err(
        "--scenario needs --severity\nusage: meta <command> [options] [--] [words]\n  concern <text> --division <path> [--source <text>] [--tag acceptance-candidate] [--severity <level>]\n  issue <text> --division <path> [--severity <level>]\n  rate <concern-id|issue-id> <level> [--scenario <text>]   (levels: the division's scale in tooling/policy.toml; raising needs the reproduction or failure scenario)\n  move <concern-id|issue-id> --division <path> [--severity <level> [--scenario <text>]]   (division: a top division or one in tooling/policy.toml; levels compare where they roll up: the level is kept only if it rolls up the same, else give --severity; a lower roll-up is free, a higher one needs --scenario)\n  open <text> --division <path> [--addresses <concern-id|issue-id>]... [--effort <tokens>] [--due <rfc3339>]\n  claim <task-id> [--from <actor>] [--worktree]   (assigns you; several may hold a task; --worktree: new worktree on branch <task-id>, prints its path)\n  claim <task-id> --agent <name>   (META_ACTOR must be set and name an actor in tooling/policy.toml [dispatch] issuers; assigns <name> with a new lease and prints its brief; start the agent with the brief as its prompt; the lease ends on release, done or retire)\n  brief <task-id> [--actor <name>] [--scratch <dir>]   (agent brief: task, setup steps and self/agent-rules.md verbatim)\n  worktrees   (this clone's worktrees: task status, missing, unrecorded)\n  gc [--dry-run]   (frees recorded worktrees whose pr is merged or closed or whose task stalled, once all work is on the remote and nothing has them open)\n  gc restore <quarantine>   (puts a stranded quarantine's file modes back, unlocks it and moves it home)\n  release <task-id>   (unassigns you)\n  done|reopen <task-id>\n  wait <task-id> --on <issue-id|task-id|review|ci|merge> [--due <rfc3339>] | resume <task-id>   (reply due: --due, else now + [liveness] reply_within in tooling/policy.toml)\n  link <task-id> <pr-number>\n  retire <id> <reason>   (won't do; keeps the entry)\n  correct <id> <text>   (replaces the entry's text)\n  list [tasks|issues|concerns] [--all]\n  status [--flags]   (divisions down to tasks, live PR and CI; --flags: flags only, exit 1 if any)\n  heartbeat tick|flags|plist   (tick: one timed run of status, writes the local snapshot, prints new flags, exit 1 if any needs judgement | flags: latest snapshot and age, stale is a flag | plist: launchd job for this clone, printed only)\n  monitor tick|report   (tick: reports this project's processes, obvious and watch tiers, into the local record, exit 1 if anything is obvious; stops nothing unless meta.local.toml [monitor] stop lists a class; also runs on heartbeat tick | report: the latest report)\n  trace last|chrome [<command>]   (latest recorded run, or the latest of <command>: last: critical path by span kind and untraced time | chrome: Chrome trace JSON; every run records to .git/meta-local/traces, META_TRACE=off skips it, meta.local.toml [trace] traces and bytes cap what stays, newest written first)\n  hook session-start|pre-tool-use|post-tool-use|stop   (Claude Code hook JSON on stdin)\n  queue run <pr-number>...   (lands each PR in order: updates it onto main, waits for checks, squash-merges it when green and clean, marks its task done as the holder once every linked PR merged; skips a conflicting PR and goes on; stops with a reason: off the default branch, base not strict, red, checks timeout, not mergeable, gh failure; exit 1 on a stop or a skip; up to about an hour per PR, so run it in the background; the hook allows it only when META_ACTOR names an actor in tooling/policy.toml [queue] landers)\n  ci-wait | ci-log   (this session's CI: wait for failure or completion | failed step output)\nactor: $META_ACTOR, else owner",
    ),
]
